<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proportion of Scores with Decreasing Trends in Data Filtering</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, we analyze the proportion of documents exhibiting a decreasing trend in translation scores. For each language pair, we compare the score of passage 1 (containing segment 1) with passage 5 (containing segments 1–5), and report (i) the total number of documents and (ii) the proportion that display a decreasing trend. The results for MetricX-24 QE are summarized in Table <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ A.1 Proportion of Scores with Decreasing Trends in Data Filtering ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Penalizing Length: Uncovering Systematic Bias in Quality Estimation Metrics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Overall, about 80% of the documents across 10 languages show a decreasing trend, indicating that length bias is pervasive in most cases.</p>
</div>
